  "mating_convention": "Face frame: origin on the mating plane at the face centre, +x = outward normal (pointing away from the rover), +z up, +y = z cross x. Two faces are mated when T_world_B*F_B = T_world_A*F_A*Rz(pi): origins coincide, outward normals are opposite, z stays up, y flips. Faces are hermaphroditic: each has two hooks (A at face y>0 on the upper level +dz, B at y<0 on the lower level -dz) and two catch pins (pin_hi at y=-yc upper level, pin_lo at y=+yc lower level) so that A's hook A closes on the opposing face's pin_hi and so on. A hook's engage_point (hook frame, closed) must coincide with the opposing catch pin position when mated.",
